Package: treehunt
Type: Package
Title: Evolutionary Search for Optimal Node Combinations in Trees
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Jules", "Bangard", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jules.bangard@etu.unistra.fr")
Author: Jules Bangard [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Jules Bangard <jules.bangard@etu.unistra.fr>
Description: Provides Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) sampling and genetic
    algorithms for searching combinations of nodes in hierarchical trees.
    Includes scores for binary outcomes, continuous outcomes, and recurrent
    events, with applications to pharmacovigilance and hospital data.
    Importance weighting estimates uniform combination score references from
    tempered MCMC samples and reports weight-based effective sample sizes.
    Computational routines are implemented in C++ via 'Rcpp'.
License: GPL-3
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.1.0), jsonlite, survival
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Encoding: UTF-8
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
URL: https://github.com/JulesBa-Git/treehunt
BugReports: https://github.com/JulesBa-Git/treehunt/issues
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), umap, dbscan, ggplot2
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: C++17
